  "starterCode": "def sql_rank_dense_rank(scores: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **RANK and DENSE_RANK** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef sql_rank_dense_rank(scores: list) -> list:\n    su = sorted(list(set(scores)), reverse=True)\n    dm = {v: i + 1 for i, v in enumerate(su)}\n    sa = sorted(scores, reverse=True)\n    rm = {}\n    for i, v in enumerate(sa):\n        if v not in rm: rm[v] = i + 1\n    return [{'score': s, 'rank': rm[s], 'dense_rank': dm[s]} for s in scores]\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
